     license, and selling it alone or as part of a bundle or a paid product.

  b. Rent or lease the Software, or sublicense it for a fee.

  c. Charge others mainly for access to the Software itself, such as offering it
     to the public as a paid hosted product.

  d. Deliver the Software or a changed version of it to a client as something
     that client pays for. You may be paid for your work, your results and your
     services, but not for a copy of the Software.


3. NAME AND COPYRIGHT

  a. You may not remove or change the name "MineOffice", the copyright notice
